      ":question/problem": "The population $P(t)$ of the town of Tinyville is given by the function\n\n$P(t) = P_{0}(\\frac{2}{3})^{t}$,\n\nwhere $t$ is the number of months since the start of a survey, and $P_{0}$ is the town's initial population. If the town's population $7$ months after the survey started was $58$, what was the initial population?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
